# Southmeadow (Docs/Design/62-talk.md, section 3): grain fields and orchards in the far south. Cheerful; harvest,
# fruit, chaff and windfalls. Drafts (phase 3), to be written properly with you (phase 7).

grammar southmeadow
greet = Good harvest | Harvest to you
greet.broad = Good 'arvest
farewell = Ripe days | Good harvest
agree = Ripe and right | Aye, ripe
refuse = Not this season
surprise = Well, pick me | Bless the barley
annoyed = Blight take it | Wormy luck
very = full
good = ripe
bad = blighted | wormy
luck = a windfall
child = sprout
pet!! = my apple | my plum
hot = sun-ripe | baking
tired = harvested
nonsense = chaff
tag = , eh
oath! = Sheaf and sickle | Blight take it | Apples and ale
home = my own orchard
